How we design gradient estimators plays an important role in convergence, particularly in asynchronous training. In this section, we first establish a general convergence bound for a broad class of gradient estimators, which shows how their second moments and bias affect the convergence. This bound will then guide us toward a principled gradient estimator that minimizes a bias upper bound while maintaining a common second-moment guarantee, thereby reducing sensitivity to asynchronous rollout delays. Lemma 1 . Suppose that θ n + 1 = θ n + η ​ g n 	heta_{n+1}=	heta_{n}+\eta g_{n} and 𝔼 [ g n ∣ ℱ n − ] = T − 1 ∇ J ( θ n ) + b n \mathbb{E}[g_{n}\mid\mathcal{F}_{n}^{-}]=T^{-1}
