This section justifies the weighting rule underlying GMC-GRPO. We first prove that the admissible mass constraint gives a uniform second-moment bound and, under coverage, bounds the correction bias by the removed importance mass. We then show that GMC uniquely maximizes retained mass among admissible direction-preserving corrections. Comparing the mass removed by GMC and TIC establishes the corresponding ordering of their certified bias envelopes, providing the basis for the convergence analysis that follows. Proof of Proposition 1 . For brevity, denote the contribution of group b b to eq. 4 by U n , b w := 1 T ​ G ∑ i = 1 G w n ( b , i ) ρ n ( b , i ) ∇ log π θ n ( y ( b , i ) ∣ x ( b ) ) A ^ ( b , i ) , g n w = 1 B ∑ b = 1 B U n , b w . U_{n,b}^{w}:= rac{1}{TG}\sum_{i=1}^{G}w_{n}^{(b,i)}ho_{n}^{(b,i)}
